[2026-11-27T11:58:51Z] note: answers: user chose (2026-11-27) to run the pair specs with a labelled assumed borrow fee on the short leg (0.25 %/yr base for easy-to-borrow ETFs/large caps, stress 1 % and 3 %) instead of disabling them as the spec requires without borrow data.
[2026-11-27T11:58:51Z] note: assumptions: Engle-Granger p-value computed in numpy exactly as statsmodels coint(trend='c', maxlag=1, autolag=None) (OLS, ADF on residuals without constant with 1 lag, MacKinnon N=2 'c' p-value constants copied from statsmodels 0.14.4); statsmodels isn't in the backtest image. Formation = the n bars before the month-end bar; the model is frozen from that month-end bar until the next one, where open positions are closed (forced) before refitting. Entry z -2 and stop z -4 are fixed constants. | BORROW COST ASSUMED (user decision 2026-11-27): the spec says to disable pairs without historical borrow/carry data; there is none, so the short leg pays a constant labelled fee (CONFIG borrow_fee_pct_yr: 0.25 %/yr for these easy-to-borrow ETFs/large caps, 3 %/yr for crypto margin) on its market value per calendar day; stress runs at higher fees are logged after the optimization. Borrow recalls and margin calls are not modelled. | short proceeds earn 0 % and the long leg is paid from the sleeve (no margin interest): conservative carry; total-return (adjusted) closes on both legs, so the short leg pays the dividends it is short (dividend-in-lieu). | gross notional G = 100 % of sleeve equity at entry (equal dollars: G/2 each; ratio 1:beta: long G/(1+beta), short beta*G/(1+beta)); quantities frozen at entry. | same-bar ambiguity: if a leg's stop is touched intrabar, that leg fills at its stop and the other leg at its worst bar extreme (long: low, short: high); if both legs touch, the long leg is assumed first. Gaps through a stop fill both legs at the open. | no new entry on a bar where a position was closed, and no entry when the exit condition (or a forced window end) is true on the signal bar. | costs: library convention (ETFs fee 0.05 % + slippage 0.03 % per fill; crypto 0.10 % + 0.10 %), both legs, entry and exit. | IAU, EWA, EWC and VDE were not in the project; their Yahoo daily history was fetched on 2026-11-27 (src.collectors.yahoo_daily.update, full history) without adding them to config/symbols.yaml, so the nightly job doesn't refresh them.
